 Invoices: usage is costed per request at list price, summed per model, converted to cents, then the key's discount is applied.
+
+## Rate limiting
+
+`createServer` accepts `rateLimit: { limit, windowMs }`. The default is `{ limit: 60, windowMs: 60000 }` (60 requests per 60000 ms). Partial options fall back to the defaults. Windows are timed with the server's `now` option.
+
+Every request except `GET /health` is limited per `x-api-key` value. The check runs before authentication and routing, so 401, 403 and 404 responses count too. Requests without the header share the key `anonymous`.
+
+Windows are fixed. A key's window starts at its first request and lasts `windowMs`. The first `limit` requests in a window are allowed and the rest are rejected. The first request at or after the window end starts a new window.
+
+A rejected request gets `429`, a `Retry-After` header (whole seconds until the window ends, rounded up, at least 1), and the body `{"error": "rate_limited", "retryAfter": <seconds>}`.
+
+Every limited response, allowed or rejected, has `X-RateLimit-Limit` and `X-RateLimit-Remaining`. Remaining is the number of requests left in the current window after this one, never below 0.
+
+`GET /health` is exempt. It is never rejected, never counted, and sent without rate-limit headers.
